>The ability to identify cursed/uncursed/blessed items is an intrinsic ability
>built in to all priestly characters from day one ( level one actually ).  It
>makes no difference what your wisdom is, nor can the ability be gained by
>other characters ( though it would be nice... )

Actually I was thinking the other day that the game would be more fun
if intrinsics weren't so easy to get.  Priests are fun to play
PRECISELY because they have this thing that no other character does.
Most of my characters look exactly the same if they win -- high str,
high dex, can't be seen, flamed, frozen, disintegrated, sued for
libel, etc., etc.

Of course it would change the game, but what if ONLY say elves and
thieves were stealthy, ONLY knights and samurais were quick, ONLY
barbarians and healers had poison resistance, etc.  Each type could
have a different combination.  At least this way all the barbarians/
wizards/valkyries/elves would look slightly different and more
important, PLAY differently thoughtout the game.

Any responses?

Allen


